<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB declines to confirm Iraq wheat purchase switch.</title>
<headline>AWB declines to confirm Iraq wheat purchase switch.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) on Wednesday said it would not confirm or deny a report that that Iraq was switching an order of 150,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat to Australia.</p>
<p>Such deals are complex and the AWB could say nothing firm on the matter, an AWB spokesman said.</p>
<p>Reuters quoted U.S. trade sources in Chicago on Tuesday as saying that Iraq was switching the order to 100,000-150,000 tonnes of Australian hard wheat.</p>
<p>The switch was probably related to price, the sources said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
